    "interpretation": "The isolated UVM path checks requested pages against the destination GPU's copy-access mask before the first migration copy is queued. A requested page resident only on an inaccessible GPU returns NV_ERR_NOT_SUPPORTED. This avoids partial GPU-to-CPU staging and a retry loop that would repeat that source stage. It intentionally does not implement cross-GPU managed-memory migration.",
